                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not wanting to sound overdramatic... But games like these while playing multiplayer. They show a glimpse of what's to come!\n\nHere's what i mean:\n\nI just played a multiplayer game with a random dude. I spawned in, looked up and saw him looking at me. He waved at me. I waved back. \n\nI didn't know what to do to start the match. So i made a shrug gesture towards him. He pointed to the table where it clearly stated what button i had to press. I pressed it and the game begun.\n\nWe played for a long time. Both of us trying different serves and screws. During the match we did all kinds of gestures towards eachother. Gestures of sadness when you lost an important point while the other celebrates with his hands in the air. Gestures of frustration when you lost a lot of points in a row etc... Body language in VR is really easy to understand. At least to me...\n\nIt was getting late and i had to go to sleep. I waved, he waved back and i disconnected. Never to see that player again...\n\nWhat's so cool about all this is that you can express yourself without any pre-programmed gestures like /wave, /dance, /whatever. Now you can make your own little dance when you win. You do your own gestures. You do you! It's magical!\n\nI can't wait for similar games like this one!\n\nI don't mention much about the actual game here except for the VR multiplayer experience.. But the game is actually really good. It feels pretty realistic. Sure it's not perfect... But it is pretty damn close i'd say.",
